new(135,"PED:US-CCSS-MATH:G2:U09:L02","https://im.kendallhunt.com/k5/teachers/grade-2/unit-9/lesson-2/preparation.html","65b106327d18820a0e2ca62b2242fb04873d806550f0ffd24119c771b41de6b3",new string[]{"CCSS:2.OA.B.2"},new string[]{"Learning goal: You will fluently add and subtract within 20 to find unknown addends.\nIn previous lessons, you assessed your fluency with sums and differences within 20. You shared different methods for finding the value of sums and differences mentally. In this lesson, you find unknown addends within 20 and continue developing fluency with addition and subtraction within 20.","Key ideas:\n- Fluently add and subtract within 20\n- In previous lessons, you assessed your fluency with sums and differences within 20\n- Subtraction can represent taking away, comparing quantities, or finding a missing addend; the representation must match the situation.","Example 1: Decide if each statement is true or false. Be prepared to explain your reasoning. \\(8 + 5 = 8 + 2 + 5\\) \\(8 + 5 = 8 + 2 + 3\\) \\(8 + 5 = 10 + 3\\)\nApproach: Represent the whole and the part, write a matching subtraction relationship, then find and check the difference.\nExample 2: Directions: Partner A holds a card on their forehead without looking. Partner B names the number that you can add to the number on the card to get 20. Partner A says the number on their card. Record an equation to represent how you found the unknown addend. my equations my partner’s equations\nApproach: Represent the whole and the part, write a matching subtraction relationship, then find and check the difference.","Step 1: Identify the whole and the part being removed or compared.\nStep 2: Represent the situation with objects, a drawing, number line, or equation.\nStep 3: Write a subtraction relationship that matches the representation.\nStep 4: Find the difference using an efficient strategy.\nStep 5: Check the result with the original quantities or a related addition fact.","Common mistake: mixing up the whole and the part being removed or compared. Check that the subtraction relationship matches the representation.","You will fluently add and subtract within 20 to find unknown addends. In previous lessons, you assessed your fluency with sums and differences within 20."},new string[]{"IM2021 G2 Unit9 Lesson2: Fluency Flip. Verified public source-specific tasks and mathematics: Warm-up verify 8+5=8+2+5 false, 8+5=8+2+3 true, 8+5=10+3 true. Source Heads Up: player holds real 0–19 card unseen; partner states a number to reach20, player guesses card. Original group Number Mix Up centers select cards. Source media and human assessment boundary: Actual original card draw, partner clue, physically held unseen value and group decisions require teacher; no predetermined official card for automated mark.","Focus: Warm-up verify 8+5=8+2+5 false, 8+5=8+2+3 true, 8+5=10+3 true. Source Heads Up: player holds real 0–19 card unseen; partner states a number to reach20, player guesses card. Original group Number Mix Up centers select cards. Standard mappings provided by ORIGINAL lesson graph: CCSS:2.OA.B.2. Original visual/physical question materials and authored open writing remain distinct from NEW Edulytics first-party numeric examples.","Actual public publisher activity: Warm-up verify 8+5=8+2+5 false, 8+5=8+2+3 true, 8+5=10+3 true. Source Heads Up: player holds real 0–19 card unseen; partner states a number to reach20, player guesses card. Original group Number Mix Up centers select cards. Independent first-party mathematical example uses different values and only exact numeric verification. Teacher separately reviews original representation or creative student problem and explanations: Actual original card draw, partner clue, physically held unseen value and group decisions require teacher; no predetermined official card for automated mark.","Step 1 Read the source question and classify its actual given/unknown quantity, chosen representation, measured unit, or student-des